"signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ca0b116ae39f1a555e2f64869e027ae3828dd9ff16a818b4bf23cb47d13e3a5e","event_uuid":"6b348109-2ab9-47d3-a32e-c1df361e0a0a","position":{"commit_sha":"c6ef85c61a9bd717b5abfebcc352e0b9b9a25329","position":"1786073288622017001-6b348109-2ab9-47d3-a32e-c1df361e0a0a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"18b51453e1d179eb139f46d661cf1f5db0b7122fb4b0c3b344e538cabd434645","event_uuid":"b5fa57c7-4474-4f2a-ae97-e5552a8c4a68","position":{"commit_sha":"f6fb5a1e562ef24fcacd7927170d18571f791c76","position":"1786075918167070001-b5fa57c7-4474-4f2a-ae97-e5552a8c4a68"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-223_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6ff494b3-b67f-4284-9d1e-818a0b7eecfd","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit 1461 ps2. First CI run was Verified-1: tests/unit/test_config_tracker_dir.py::test_reads_tracker_dir_validation_gate_rejects_non_git_root pinned the OLD sys.exit behaviour and had to be updated as part of this change (now expects TrackerRootError). My pre-flight had only run tests/interfaces -- gap closed by running the full tests/unit suite (8699 passed).\n\nDesign note worth keeping: the end-to-end CLI path never reached the sys.exit sites. _cli/_init.py auto-init refuses a non-repo cwd BEFORE dispatch and emits the same message, so an uninitialized-cwd CLI test proves nothing here. An earlier version of my test asserted exactly that and was VACUOUS -- caught by changing the message to a sentinel and observing the CLI still print the original. The CLI mapping is now tested by making dispatch raise directly. Residual real triggers: explicit non-repo root, repo vanishing mid-session.\n\nUnrelated pre-existing failure observed and cleared: tests/unit/metrics/test_jscpd_dup_heldout.py::test_live_clone fails identically with my changes stashed (environmental, needs the jscpd tool).","timestamp":1786073288622017001}],"created_at":1786046997702443001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"3d3e42e5-ae3b-41f0-a255-45df696afd6a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"59a7-957f-749e-44a9"},{"link_uuid":"edffcebd-0d58-4706-a81c-732c87433f13","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e67b-8dd9-51b5-44dd"},{"link_uuid":"54b8c17b-3fa4-44c6-94d3-ef06c70f3b34","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"78c0-61a0-fe46-4f03"}],"description":"`_engine_support/reads.py:133-137` and `:151-157` print to stderr and call `sys.exit(1)` when the\nrepo root is not a git worktree. That function is reached from the library gate surface\n(`_lib_gates.py:42,68,83,109,118,163,210`) and thence from MCP (`_mcp_reads.py:212,218,224`).\n\nEmpirically proven during verification: a real in-memory FastMCP client was driven against a tool\nthat exits this way. FastMCP catches `Exception` (`mcp/server/fastmcp/tools/base.py:116`) and\n`SystemExit` is a `BaseException`, so the whole `anyio.run` dies — the MCP server PROCESS\nterminates rather than returning a tool error.\n\nTrigger is narrow (REBAR_ROOT unset with a non-repo cwd, or the repo vanishing mid-session), but a\nleaf helper unilaterally deciding process lifetime for every embedding surface is the defect. The\nlibrary contract is to raise `RebarError`.\n\nBoth remediation proposers converged: convert to a domain exception and map it to exit 1 at the CLI\nboundary ONLY, so the CLI's observable behaviour is unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `tracker_dir()` raises a rebar error instead of calling `sys.exit`\n- [x] The CLI maps that error to exit 1 with the same message as today\n- [x] A test asserts an MCP tool returns an error payload (not a dead server) with REBAR_ROOT unset in a non-repo cwd\n- [x] No `sys.exit` remains reachable from `_lib_*` or `_mcp_*`","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","b5bc-f4f7-3433-4181"],["relates_to","59a7-957f-749e-44a9"],["relates_to","78c0-61a0-fe46-4f03"],["relates_to","e67b-8dd9-51b5-44dd"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"b5bc-f4f7-3433-4181","parent_status_uuid":"0b9f1224-7c6a-42c9-b3fd-e0a527a801ab","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["janitor"],"ticket_id":"176d-6bb4-df56-49cd","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Remove sys.exit from the shared read core","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["74c6fb6f-bc8d-4cb6-97e0-90211b3d6242","0b9f1224-7c6a-42c9-b3fd-e0a527a801ab","dd266a11-d11f-408c-8b12-88c247499d98","3d3e42e5-ae3b-41f0-a255-45df696afd6a","6b348109-2ab9-47d3-a32e-c1df361e0a0a","edffcebd-0d58-4706-a81c-732c87433f13","b5fa57c7-4474-4f2a-ae97-e5552a8c4a68","54b8c17b-3fa4-44c6-94d3-ef06c70f3b34"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786088742343140108,"uuid":"cb1e1e98-d03d-4496-a5e8-2c27b5bea1fc"}